                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3e9b6b1-dc78-3b5b-b5fd-ea8697174722",
                                        "entry_id": "70cbeaa0-61dd-3bf3-a377-226875a3e816",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or process of holding fast; that which serves to hold fast."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27cec513-dfd2-4994-b55c-48f1ae0fca4a",
                                                "sense_id": "c3e9b6b1-dc78-3b5b-b5fd-ea8697174722",
                                                "text": "to get a good clinch of an antagonist, or of a weapon"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "695b0974-0c64-490d-bde1-bc9aebd79271",
                                                "sense_id": "c3e9b6b1-dc78-3b5b-b5fd-ea8697174722",
                                                "text": "to secure anything by a clinch"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e139288e-f28f-33a9-ac4b-c48d171e01e0",
                                        "entry_id": "70cbeaa0-61dd-3bf3-a377-226875a3e816",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b2101a45-13cb-33e8-ab01-4d2002f87c82",
                                        "entry_id": "70cbeaa0-61dd-3bf3-a377-226875a3e816",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hitch or bend by which a rope is made fast to the ring of an anchor, or the breeching of a ship's gun to the ringbolts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec0a787c-6ca0-30bb-96ed-b2e0202ca550",
                                        "entry_id": "70cbeaa0-61dd-3bf3-a377-226875a3e816",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A passionate embrace."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b5aead0-4075-4fad-b394-931c54238cb2",
                                                "sense_id": "ec0a787c-6ca0-30bb-96ed-b2e0202ca550",
                                                "text": "More likely, he was letting her know that his visit this morning was not going to end in a clinch—or something steamier. It was going to be about sitting at a table, drinking coffee and talking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92ba9195-5089-4a8e-9409-a414027fa171",
                                                "sense_id": "ec0a787c-6ca0-30bb-96ed-b2e0202ca550",
                                                "text": "So, then, to the health secretary’s “steamy clinch” with Gina Coladangelo, the lobbyist and long-term friend he took on as an aide last year […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5336fb2-b93e-36da-92a8-95802fb775fc",
                                        "entry_id": "70cbeaa0-61dd-3bf3-a377-226875a3e816",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of one or both fighters holding onto the other to prevent being hit or engage in standup grappling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34190bd5-8827-3f80-afb2-38ef8d3b91ca",
                                        "entry_id": "70cbeaa0-61dd-3bf3-a377-226875a3e816",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prison sentence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d43dc2c-5e3c-4fd9-829c-fb9f7ef9b437",
                                                "sense_id": "34190bd5-8827-3f80-afb2-38ef8d3b91ca",
                                                "text": "COOMBE: He got the clinch only last week — eighteen months. You see it's no good having anybody here as ain't got a^([sic]) unblemished character. We don't want to have the bluebottles come sniffing round here, do we?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
